```

This will create a new `csv` service in the `services` directory.

### Step 4: Implement the CSV service

In the `csv` service, we will use a web worker to download the CSV file. We will create a new worker script that will handle the downloading of the CSV file.

```javascript
// services/csv.js
import { Worker } from 'worker_threads';

export default class CsvService {
  async downloadCsv(csvData) {
    const worker = new Worker('./workers/download-csv.js', {
      workerData: csvData,
    });

    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
      worker.on('message', (data) => {
        resolve(data);
      });

      worker.on('error', (error) => {
        reject(error);
      });
    });
  }
}
